  "description": "<p>Long Island University Brooklyn is a private university in Brooklyn, New York. It is the first of two main campuses of the private Long Island University system. The University is ranked number one for health professional majors. Around 700 international students from more than 75 countries travel to use the Universityâ€™s state-of-the-art facilities and world-class teaching.</p><h2>What is the Long Island University Brooklyn acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The Long Island University Brooklyn acceptance rate is 85%.</p> <p>The University has numerous academic buildings, including the Humanities Building, Health Sciences Building, and the Pratt Building, which contains the School of Arts and Communication. Students have access to athletic facilities via outdoor soccer fields, basketball courts, and tennis courts. The Steinberg Wellness Center features a gymnasium, fitness center, swimming pool, and more. The Kumble Theater for the Performing Arts, the Arnold and Marie Schwartz Athletic Center, and the Salena Gallery are all performance venues with exciting facilities.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>The campus experience fair enables students to peruse the variety of student clubs on campus and make connections. Students join together across around 200 student clubs that reflect various interests. Students can access multiple campus activities and events from Spring Book Club to Move It Monday. One of the fastest-growing Greek communities in the nation can be found at the Long Island University Brooklyn campus, and it is recognised as a top 100 National University for social mobility. Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion councils create an inclusive student environment.</p>",
