      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Long Island University Brooklyn is a private university in Brooklyn, New York. It is the first of two main campuses of the private Long Island University system. The University is ranked number one for health professional majors. Around 700 international students from more than 75 countries travel to use the University's state-of-the-art facilities and world-class teaching.</p><p>The University has numerous academic buildings, including the Humanities Building, Health Sciences Building, and the Pratt Building, which contains the School of Arts and Communication. The Kumble Theater for the Performing Arts, the Arnold and Marie Schwartz Athletic Center, and the Salena Gallery are all performance venues with exciting facilities.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "image": null,
